/-!
# `K₀` of dg rings whose low-degree cohomology is that of `ℤ`

Let `A` be a dg ring such that `Hⁿ(A) = 0` for `n < 0` and for `n = 1`, `H⁰(A) ≅ ℤ`, and `H²(A)`
is torsion-free (`DG.DGRing.K0.IntegralLowDegree`; for instance `A` concentrated in non-negative
degrees with `A⁰ = ℤ · 1`, `DG.IsConnectedInt`, `H¹(A) = 0` and `H²(A)` torsion-free). Then every
compact object of `D(A)` has a heart tower whose cells are the derived inductions of shifted finitely
generated abelian groups along `ℤ → A`, and the Grothendieck group `K₀(A)` of compact objects is
generated by the class `[A]` (`DG.DGRing.K0.exists_eq_zsmul_self`). If moreover `A` has a morphism
of dg rings to `ℤ` (an augmentation, e.g. `DG.IsConnectedInt.augmentation`), then `K₀(A) ≃ ℤ` with
`[A] ↦ 1` (`DG.DGRing.K0.equivIntOfAugmentation`, `DG.DGRing.K0.equivIntOfIsConnectedInt`).

This is an integral counterpart of `K₀(A) ≅ K₀(A⁰)` for positive dg rings (`A⁰` semisimple,
`DG.IsPositive`), which does not apply when `A⁰ = ℤ`. The proof applies
`DG.IntegralHeart.exists_eq_zsmul` (`DG/Derived/IntegralHeart.lean`) to the triangulated functor
`D(Mod ℤ) ≌ D(ℤ) ⥤ D(A)` (Mathlib's derived category of abelian groups, the comparison equivalence
`DG.DegreeZero.derivedComparisonEquivalence`, and derived induction along the unit `ℤ → A`), which
sends `ℤ` in degree `0` to `A` (`DG.DGRingHom.derivedInductionSelfIso`). Its hypotheses are read
off `Hom_{D(A)}(A, A⟦n⟧) ≅ Hⁿ(A)` (`DG.DerivedCategory.homSelfShiftAddEquiv`), and `End(A)` is
generated by the identity because it is a ring whose additive group is infinite cyclic
(`DG.isUnit_of_addEquiv_int`).

## Main results

* `DG.DerivedCategory.homShiftAddEquivOfIsKProjective`: `Hom_{D(A)}(P, N⟦n⟧) ≃+ Hⁿ(HOM_A(P, N))`
  for a K-projective `P`; `DG.DerivedCategory.homSelfShiftAddEquiv`: `Hom(A, A⟦n⟧) ≃+ Hⁿ(A)`.
* `DG.DGRingHom.extendScalarsSelfEquiv`, `DG.DGRingHom.derivedInductionSelfIso`: `A ⊗_B B ≅ A`
  and `φ^*(B) ≅ A` for a morphism of dg rings `φ : B → A`.
* `DG.DegreeZero.intHom A : ℤ →ᵈᵍ+* A`, the unit.
* `DG.IsConnectedInt`, `DG.IsConnectedInt.cohomologyZeroEquiv` (`H⁰(A) ≃ ℤ`),
  `DG.IsConnectedInt.augmentation` (`A → ℤ`, `a ↦ a₀`).
* `DG.DGRing.K0.exists_eq_zsmul_self`, `DG.DGRing.K0.equivIntOfAugmentation`,
  `DG.DGRing.K0.equivIntOfIsConnectedInt`.
-/


